---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import JoinBuilder from '../../components/JoinBuilder.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="SQL JOIN Builder" description="Build a JOIN query visually — pick tables, join type, and matching keys.">
  <JoinBuilder client:load slot="tool" />
  <h2>Choosing the right join type</h2>
  <p>INNER JOIN returns only matching rows in both tables. LEFT JOIN keeps all rows from the left table even without a match. RIGHT JOIN does the reverse. FULL OUTER JOIN keeps all rows from both, matched or not.</p>

  <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Using INNER JOIN when you actually need LEFT JOIN</strong>, silently dropping rows that don't have a match instead of showing them with NULLs.</li>
    <li><strong>Forgetting join conditions</strong>, accidentally producing a cross join (every row matched with every row) that returns far more rows than intended.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Use cases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Combining data from related tables in a report query</li>
    <li>Finding records in one table that don't have a corresponding match in another (via LEFT JOIN with NULL check)</li>
    <li>Learning join type differences with a visual builder</li>
  </ul>
</ToolLayout>
